    {{ 'base.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {%- comment -%}
      SHEmakes redesign layer. Loaded after base.css so it restyles the theme
      rather than forking it — removing these two lines reverts the site to
      stock Boho Dream, which is what makes the redesign reviewable.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {{ 'shemakes.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {%- comment -%}
      The palette, from Theme settings → SHEmakes colours.

      shemakes.css never names a colour directly — it names a token — so
      redefining the tokens here repaints the whole redesign from the theme
      editor. This sits after the stylesheet on purpose: same specificity as
      its `:root`, later in the document, so it wins.

      The hairlines, the faint text and the three shadows are mixed from the
      text colour rather than being settings of their own. They have to stay
      in key with it, and two pickers that must agree is one picker too many.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <style>
      :root {
