    <script src="{{ 'shemakes.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- comment -%}
      The React islands. A module, which is deferred by default, so it never
      blocks the Liquid page it is enhancing — every island has a
      server-rendered fallback inside its own mount point.

      It has to be `type="module"`, not a plain deferred script. Vite emits
      top-level `var`s with one-letter names, and in a classic script every
      one of them is a property of window. An app on the page assigned its
      own global `i` — the name React's JSX runtime had been given — and the
      review carousel crashed with "i.jsx is not a function" the next time it
      rendered, leaving Judge.me's own header showing in its place. A module
      keeps those names to itself.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="module" src="{{ 'shemakes-islands.js' | asset_url }}"></script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Satoshi, Playfair Display and JetBrains Mono — the pairing this theme
      was drawn with. Satoshi sets the sentence, Playfair the part being
      emphasised, JetBrains Mono the labels. Inter, Montserrat and two scripts
      were tried over the top of it and taken back out: the shop asked for the
      original set, on the grounds that a customer has to read it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Cooper BT, the shop's own licensed file, bundled with the theme: it is
      the first thing read on every page, and a webfont that arrives late is a
      heading that changes shape while it is being read. Bold, not Black —
      the same letterforms with air left inside them, which is what a page of
      headings needs and a logo does not.

      Converted to woff2 from the supplied TrueType — 225KB down to 66KB, and
      it is the format every browser in use reads.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preload" as="font" href="{{ 'cooper-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <style>
      @font-face {
        font-family: 'Cooper BT';
        src: url({{ 'cooper-bold.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
        font-weight: 400 900;
        font-style: normal;
        font-display: swap;
      }

      @font-face {
        font-family: 'Cooper BT Medium';
        src: url({{ 'cooper-medium.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
        font-weight: 400 600;
        font-style: normal;
        font-display: swap;
      }
    </style>

